\text{LHS} = \frac{2\sin x\cos x}{\sin x} - \frac{2\cos^2 x - 1}{\cos x}
= 2\cos x - 2\cos x + \frac{1}{\cos x}
= \frac{1}{\cos x} = \text{RHS}

Marking guideline (3 marks, award the highest band the response fully meets):
- Complete proof (3 marks)
- Correct substitutions with an error in simplifying (2 marks)
- One correct double angle substitution (1 mark)
Equivalent methods and wording that show the same understanding get the same marks.

